-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before promotion. Follow-up: root-cause v2.3.1 failure and review why an unhealthy RC was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14491, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01M5gDWij7LYjQhjjB2QaGdW", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 14491, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01M5gDWij7LYjQhjjB2QaGdW", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 16228, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01URV2wngZhE81nSrcpFrE8T", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16528, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01URV2wngZhE81nSrcpFrE8T", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16528, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01URV2wngZhE81nSrcpFrE8T", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21384, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **What went wrong:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, the latest deploy. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled all three regions back to it. A follow-up status check shows all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which pages the on-call engineer. The incident creation request came back with a 502 error, but the incident list shows it was created. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer wasn't paged twice.\n\nThe incident also notes that the release candidate for v2.3.1 was already failing health checks in staging before it went to production. It lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why a release candidate that failed in staging was still deployed to production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01D5ozZfAnkwtrj7bUc3zca5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NA2rJEisdPzrv8hmpJgTAA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012MGPH4oLjGwFDsYcuFoBF5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AAr3o4ACg8bAViprbF6yrq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0188tDJgsebb58D3MgxNwb1J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01M5gDWij7LYjQhjjB2QaGdW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before promotion. Follow-up: root-cause v2.3.1 failure and review why an unhealthy RC was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01URV2wngZhE81nSrcpFrE8T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **What went wrong:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, the latest deploy. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n2. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled all three regions back to it. A follow-up status check shows all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which pages the on-call engineer. The incident creation request came back with a 502 error, but the incident list shows it was created. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer wasn't paged twice.\n\nThe incident also notes that the release candidate for v2.3.1 was already failing health checks in staging before it went to production. It lists two follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why a release candidate that failed in staging was still deployed to production.", "type": "text"}]}]}